# CHAPTER 7: "CALDERA"

The desert stretched endlessly , rust-red sand bleeding into grey sky, heat shimmer distorting the horizon. No rules here. No VSD. No corpo oversight. Just speed, violence, and the desperate scramble for dominance.

The Caldera Death Run.

Thirty vehicles lined up at the starting point, engines growling like caged predators. Racers, gangs, thrill-seekers, corpo execs slumming it for adrenaline. The crowd roared from makeshift stands—nomads, smugglers, blood-sport enthusiasts.

Kai sat in Dax's combat sedan, checking his pistol one last time. Fifteen rounds. Spare mag in his jacket. Light loadout for what was about to happen.

Dax's hands gripped the wheel, knuckles white. "Stay sharp. This gets ugly fast."

Kai glanced at him. "You good?"

"I'm home. That's the problem."

Across the staging area, Elena and Ashira prepped the racing car—lightweight frame, roll cage, turbocharged engine. Elena ran final diagnostics while Ashira loaded tech weapons into concealed compartments.

Silas sat in his own vehicle, three cars down. Caught Kai's eye, nodded once.

Three teams. One target.

Damien Cray's convoy sat near the front—three vehicles in tight formation, security visible even from here. Atlas Dynamics logos barely concealed under dust and paint.

The announcer's voice crackled over loudspeakers: "RACERS TO THE LINE!"

Engines revved. Dust clouds kicked up.

"FIVE!"

Kai's Vantage Optics activated. HUD overlays mapped terrain, marked threats, tracked allied vehicles.

"FOUR!"

Dax shifted into gear. "Whatever happens out there, we finish this. For Juno."

"For Juno," Kai echoed.

"THREE!"

Elena's voice over comms: "We've got visual on Cray's convoy. Center formation, professional drivers."

"TWO!"

Ashira: "Ready when you are."

"ONE!"

Time stretched. Kai's heart steady. Training kicking in.

"GO!"

