## ACT 3: CORNERING CRAY

The canyon passage was perfect. Narrow, walled on both sides, only one way through.

Cray's vehicle raced into it, desperate to escape.

Elena blocked the far exit. Dax pushed from behind. Silas cut off the side routes.

Trapped.

Cray's driver tried to reverse. Too late. Silas rammed him from the side, pinning the vehicle against the canyon wall.

"Out of the vehicle!" Kai shouted. "Now!"

The doors opened. Four men emerged—three security guards, one corpo exec in expensive augments and designer jacket.

Damien Cray. Target confirmed.

The guards raised weapons.

Kai's Surge activated.

Not full Ghost state—just combat enhancement. Time dilated. His HUD flooded with tactical data.

**"HOSTILE COUNT: FOUR. THREAT LEVEL: MINIMAL. OPTIMAL ENGAGEMENT PROTOCOL LOADED."**

The Voice. Calm, tactical, not quite his own thoughts.

Kai moved.

First guard: Disarm, strike to throat, down.

Second guard: Dodge fire, close distance, blade to kidney, down.

Third guard: Attempted to flank, Kai predicted it, leg sweep, knockout blow.

Ten seconds. Three guards neutralized.

The Voice: **"EFFICIENCY: 92%. ACCEPTABLE. FINAL TARGET: EXECUTIVE. NON-COMBATANT. TERMINATE?"**

Kai ignored it. Holstered his weapon.

Cray stood alone, hands raised. "Wait! Wait! I can pay you! Whatever you're getting, I'll triple it!"

Elena approached, Data Tap interface glowing. "I'm not here for your money."

She pressed her wrist port to the vehicle's access panel. Neural handshake. Systems breached.

Ninety seconds.

Cray kept talking. "You don't understand! That data is classified! Atlas will hunt you! You'll never be safe!"

Kai stepped forward. "We're already being hunted. For what you did. What Atlas did."

"I don't know what you—"

"The Surge. The testing. Ashen Reach. All of it."

Cray went pale.

Elena: "Download complete. Got everything."

Ashira appeared, katana drawn but not raised. Silent presence. Threat understood.

Cray looked between them. "You're making a mistake. Atlas Dynamics doesn't forgive. They erase."

"Then we'll burn them before they get the chance," Elena said.

Kai turned to leave. "Leave him. He's not worth it."

They moved toward their vehicles.

Cray exhaled. Thought he'd survived.

Then Silas appeared.

Cray froze. "You. You're the oneâ€""

Silas walked up calmly. Gun already drawn.

"Wait! I told you everything! I cooperatedâ€""

Silas stuck the barrel in Cray's mouth.

"You people never learn."

BANG.

Cray dropped.

The crew froze. Stared.

Silas holstered his weapon, turned to face them. Not apologetic. Not aggressive. Just matter-of-fact.

"You leave them alive, they come back with armies. Atlas doesn't forgive. They erase."

He looked at Kai specifically. "Loose ends get people killed. Like Juno."

Pause.

"Don't make that mistake again."

Silas walked back to his vehicle.

Kai stood there, processing. Elena and Ashira exchanged glances.

Dax finally spoke: "Nomads have a saying: 'A wounded enemy is a future problem.'"

Elena: "He's not wrong."

Ashira said nothing. Didn't need to.

Kai looked at Cray's body. Then at Silas driving away.

"Let's move. We've got company incoming."

