## ACT 4: ESCAPE & COMPLICATIONS

The pursuit came fast.

Atlas reinforcements—must have been on standby, waiting for Cray's signal. Four vehicles, heavily armed, professional drivers.

"Split up!" Kai ordered over comms. "Confuse the pursuit!"

Elena: "Ashira and I will head back to Veyline. Fastest route. We've got the data."

Silas: "I'll draw some off. Got my own exit strategy."

That left Kai and Dax. Combat sedan against four Atlas vehicles.

"Think we can take them?" Kai asked.

"Not a chance. But I can lose them." Dax grinned—first real smile since Kade. "This is nomad territory. They're not."

He punched the accelerator, turned hard off the main circuit.

The Atlas vehicles followed. Two broke off to chase Elena. One went after Silas.

One stayed on Kai and Dax.

The chase became a desperate scramble through Caldera's deep desert. Dax drove like he was possessed—reading terrain by instinct, taking routes that shouldn't exist, using every nomad trick he'd ever learned.

The Atlas vehicle kept pace. Professional driver. Good equipment.

Kai returned fire through the shattered rear window. Hit their windshield, their tires, their engine block.

Nothing stopped them.

"Dax, we need to lose them NOW!"

"I know a place. Hold on!"

Dax turned into what looked like a dead-end canyon. Atlas vehicle followed.

Then Dax yanked the wheel, threading through a gap in the rocks barely wide enough for the sedan.

The Atlas vehicle tried to follow. Didn't make it. Crashed into the canyon wall with a screech of metal.

Silence.

Dax kept driving. Deeper into the wasteland. Away from main routes, away from civilization.

"Where are we going?"

"Somewhere they won't follow. Somewhere we can hide until this blows over."

Twenty minutes later, they found it.

