## ACT 5: THE SETTLEMENT

The old nomad camp sat in a shallow valley, hidden from main routes. Maybe ten structures—prefab shelters, rusted vehicles, weathered tarps.

Half were empty. A few had squatters.

Dax parked the sedan behind a collapsed structure. Shut off the engine.

Silence. Just wind and settling metal.

Kai assessed the damage. Rear quarter panel crumpled. Tires shredded. Engine overheating. They'd made it. Barely.

Dax sat there, staring at the steering wheel.

"You good?" Kai asked.

"Used to camp here. When I was a kid. Whole clan. Every summer we'd come through Caldera, set up here for a few weeks. Trade, rest, repair vehicles." He smiled, but it was broken. "Before the ambush."

"Dax—"

"Kade tried to kill us today. My oldest friend. Brother, practically." He looked at Kai. "Does it ever stop? The guilt?"

Kai thought about Juno. About his brother. About the massacre.

"No. But you learn to carry it."

Dax nodded slowly.

They sat in silence. Two survivors processing trauma in a dead camp.

Kai's comms pinged. Encrypted channel.

"Kai, it's Ashira."

"Status?"

"Elena and I made it out. Data's secure. Heading back to Veyline now."

"Good. We're holed up in Caldera. Vehicle's damaged. Might be a day before we can move."

"Understood. One more thing."

Pause.

"The data. I've been reviewing it. There's a name you should know."

Kai's chest tightened. "What name?"

"Someone matching your brother's description. Operating in Ashen Reach. Part of the Surge Containment Grid."

The world stopped.

"Kai? You there?"

"...Yeah. Send me everything you have."

"Will do. Be safe."

The line went dead.

Kai sat there, staring at nothing.

Brother. Alive. In Ashen Reach.

Part of SCG—the unit that hunted Surge users like him.

Everything connected. The massacre. The Surge. Ashen Reach. His brother.

Dax noticed. "Bad news?"

"Maybe. Maybe good. I don't know yet."

"Want to talk about it?"

Kai touched the pendant under his shirt. "My brother. I thought he was dead. Just found out he's alive. In Ashen Reach."

Dax processed that. "The city we've been avoiding."

"Yeah."

"And now?"

"Now I think we need to go there."

Before Dax could respond, another vehicle approached.

They tensed. Hands on weapons.

Silas's car rolled up. Parked. He got out.

"You followed us?" Kai asked.

"Doubled back after losing my tail. Saw you head this way." Silas looked at their sedan. "You're not making it to Veyline in that."

"We'll manage."

"Or you can ride with me. I'm heading back anyway."

"Why help us?"

"Because you took bullets for me once. And because..." He paused. "I want to visit Juno's memorial. At the Remembrance Nexus. I owe him that."

Dax's expression softened. "You knew Juno?"

"He's the one who connected me with Vera. Before everything went to shit. He was... good people."

"Yeah," Kai said quietly. "He was."

Moment of shared grief. Three men who'd lost someone.

"So?" Silas asked. "You coming or staying?"

Kai looked at Dax. Dax looked at their ruined sedan.

"Alright. We ride with you."

