## ACT 6: RETURN TO VEYLINE

The drive back was quiet. Three men in one vehicle, each processing their own demons.

Desert gave way to industrial decay. Decay gave way to city lights. Veyline City emerged on the horizon—neon bleeding into night, corpo towers watching over everything.

Home.

Silas broke the silence. "I'll visit the Nexus tomorrow. You coming?"

Kai thought about Juno. About the messages waiting there. About debts unpaid.

"Yeah. I should."

They reached Edgehaven as night deepened. Silas dropped them off near Kai's apartment.

"Tomorrow, then," Silas said.

"Tomorrow."

Dax walked off toward his own place. Shoulders heavy. Still carrying Kade's betrayal.

Kai stood alone in the street. Looked up at his building.

Mira was inside. Safe. Sleeping. Unaware of everything that had happened.

He needed to keep it that way.

---

## ACT 7: HOME

Mira was asleep. Drawings taped to the wall, crayons scattered on her desk. Peaceful.

Stitch waited in the kitchen. Tea already brewed.

"You're alive," Stitch said.

"Barely."

"The Surge?"

"Activated. I controlled it. Mostly."

Stitch studied him. "Mostly isn't good enough."

"It's all I have."

They sat in silence. Stitch poured tea. Kai drank. Warmth spreading through exhausted limbs.

"I found something," Kai finally said. "About my brother."

Stitch set his cup down. "What?"

"He's alive. In Ashen Reach. Part of the Surge Containment Grid."

Stitch absorbed that. "The unit that hunts people like you."

"Yeah."

"What are you going to do?"

"I don't know. But I need to find him. Need answers. Need to understand what happened that night."

"Going back to Ashen Reach—that's where the massacre happened. Where the trauma triggers—"

"I know."

"The Surge could activate. Full Ghost state. In the one place that broke you."

"I'll manage."

"Will you? Or will you become that thing again?"

Kai had no answer.

Stitch sighed. "Take the crew. Don't go alone. They've seen what you can do. They'll help."

"I will."

Kai stood, walked to Mira's room. Watched her sleep for a long moment.

She was growing. Still young, still innocent. Still his reason for staying human.

He touched the pendant under his shirt. Brother's pendant.

Two brothers. One he thought was dead. One hunting people with the same curse Kai carried.

Ashen Reach. Where it all started.

Where it would all end.

