## ACT 8: BROTHER'S DOMAIN

[ASHEN REACH - BLOOD ARENA DISTRICT - ABANDONED INDUSTRIAL COMPLEX]

The training floor sprawled below—twenty-five operatives drilling in coordinated chaos. Wrestling. Boxing. Hand-to-hand combat. Brutal. Efficient. Disciplined.

Brother watched from the elevated platform, arms crossed. Cold assessment.

One operative failed a drill—too slow, too hesitant. Brother noted it. Didn't react. Just filed it away for later correction.

Another succeeded—perfect form, brutal efficiency. Slight nod. Approval earned.

The eagle perched beside him on a reinforced stand.

**Hayate.** 疾風. Swift wind.

Both eyes augmented—glowing optics, camera feeds, night vision, targeting overlays. The eagle's vision fed directly into Brother's Vantage Optics. Split-screen reality: Training floor below, aerial view of Ashen Reach rooftops above.

Brother's HUD flickered. Encrypted message incoming.

**SOURCE: [CLASSIFIED]**

**CONTENT: KAI REYES. CALDERA OPERATION. ATLAS DATA BREACH CONFIRMED. MOVEMENT DETECTED.**

He processed the information.

Three years. Three years hunting the Atlas operatives who'd left them to die. Tracking them across the continent. Eliminating them one by one.

And now Kai was moving.

Brother looked at Hayate. His optics pulsed—subtle gesture, neural command transmitted.

The eagle's augmented eyes flared in response. Understood.

Hayate spread wings—massive, enhanced, deadly—and launched from the platform. Disappeared into Ashen Reach's rain-soaked sky.

Brother watched through split vision: His own eyes on the training floor, Hayate's eyes soaring over the city.

Predator's view. Watching. Waiting.

His second-in-command approached. "Sir?"

"Kai Reyes. Inbound to Ashen Reach. Timeline: One week. Possibly less."

"Orders?"

"Eyes on every entry point. Vehicle checkpoints, nomad routes, underground access. When he arrives, I know immediately."

"And if we encounter him?"

Brother's expression didn't change. "No engagement. No interference. I handle this personally."

"Understood, sir."

The operative left.

Brother turned back to the training floor. Another drill. Another operative proving themselves.

Through Hayate's eyes, he saw Ashen Reach spread below. Every street, every district, every shadow. His territory now. His domain.

Three years ago, he'd been left to die in an arena. Forced to decapitate a man to prove his loyalty. Made into a monster to survive.

And Kai had run. Saved himself. Left him bleeding.

That's what Brother believed. What he'd convinced himself of through three years of blood and violence.

Now Kai was coming back.

Good.

Rain fell harder. Hayate circled above the city, unbothered.

Brother spoke quietly to himself, words lost in the training floor noise below:

"Come home, Kai."

Not welcome. Not forgiveness.

Just inevitability.

Two brothers. Two ghosts born the same night. Both shaped by the same massacre.

Only one would walk away from Ashen Reach.

Brother watched his forces train. Watched Hayate patrol his sky. Watched the city wait.

He was ready.
